# Language detection on GitHub.
*.proto linguist-detectable=true

# Map custom extension to Protocol Buffer
*.protobuf linguist-language=Protocol Buffer

# Everything below is compared byte-for-byte by the test suite, so git must not
# rewrite it on checkout. Without these, git's default core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows turns every committed LF into CRLF and the comparison fails on the line
# ending alone.
#
# The .proto *inputs* are pinned as well as the expected outputs, and not only
# because the golden harness reads them: doc comments are lifted out of proto
# source and forwarded into generated output, so a CRLF checkout of an input file
# can put a stray \r in the middle of a golden line rather than only at the end of
# one — which reads as a content mismatch, not a line-ending one.
*.proto text eol=lf

# Golden fixtures: case inputs and expected output trees.
#
# The pattern is repo-relative and has no leading directory: this file lives at
# the root of the cache repository, so "target/..." is right and
# "cache/target/..." silently matches nothing. Verify a change here with
# `git check-attr text eol -- <a golden file>` rather than by eye — a pattern
# that matches nothing looks exactly like one that works until a CRLF checkout
# breaks every byte comparison at once.
plugin/generator/testdata/** text eol=lf

# Committed generated output. `just regen` rewrites it with LF, so a CRLF
# checkout would show every line of every file as modified.
examples/generated/** text eol=lf
